<title>ROMANIA: Romanian leu closes slightly firmer at 6,200/900.</title>
<headline>Romanian leu closes slightly firmer at 6,200/900.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's leu closed Friday firming slightly at 6,200/900 to the dollar, from its opening level of 6,700/7,000, on a calm interbank market.</p>
<p>Romania's central bank (BNR) said it had calculated the exchange rate of the leu, used mainly for statistical purposes, at 6,890 to the dollar for March 21.</p>
<p>Short-term rates were around 220-223 percent in a fairly liquid money market, operators said.</p>
<p>Leu-dollar retail prices hovered around 6,750/7,300.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
